<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy | Kingdom Roe Coaching & Consulting"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Kingdom Roe Coaching & Consulting collects, uses and protects your personal information."
  updated="November 24, 2026"
>
  <p>Naomi Roe LLC, doing business as Kingdom Roe Coaching &amp; Consulting (“Kingdom Roe,” “we,” “us” or “our”), respects your privacy. This policy explains what information we collect when you visit kingdomroe.com, take one of our quizzes or assessments, join our email list, apply for or purchase one of our programs, and how we use and protect that information.</p>
  <p>By using this website, you agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p><strong>Information you give us.</strong> We collect the information you choose to share with us, such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and email address when you join our email list, take a quiz or download a free resource.</li>
    <li>Your quiz and assessment answers and results, when you choose to send them to us.</li>
    <li>Information you share when you apply to work with us or book a call, such as your business, your goals and your answers to application questions.</li>
    <li>Billing details when you make a purchase. Payments are processed by third-party payment processors. We do not store your full card number.</li>
    <li>Anything you send us by email or share during coaching sessions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider automatically receives basic technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type, device type and the pages you view. This helps keep the site secure and working properly.</p>

  <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To deliver what you asked for, such as your quiz results, free resources, programs and coaching services.</li>
    <li>To send you emails, including teaching, encouragement, program updates and offers. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link at the bottom of any email.</li>
    <li>To review your application and schedule calls with you.</li>
    <li>To process payments and manage your enrollment.</li>
    <li>To answer your questions and serve you well.</li>
    <li>To improve our website, content and programs.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to anyone.</p>

  <h2>Services We Use</h2>
  <p>We use trusted third-party services to run our business. They may process your information on our behalf, under their own privacy policies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, to host and protect this website.</li>
    <li><strong>Flodesk</strong>, to send our emails and host some of our sales and checkout pages.</li>
    <li><strong>Calendly</strong>, to schedule calls and receive applications.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>, to display the fonts on this website.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment processors</strong>, to securely process your payments.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies. The services listed above, such as our scheduling, email and checkout pages, may use their own cookies when you use them. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>How We Protect Your Information</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable steps to keep your information safe, and our website is served over a secure, encrypted connection. Still, no method of sending or storing information online is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>Confidentiality in Coaching</h2>
  <p>What you share with us during coaching and cohort sessions is held in confidence. We will not share your personal story without your permission. We share testimonials only with the client’s consent.</p>

  <h2>How Long We Keep Your Information</h2>
  <p>We keep your information for as long as we need it to serve you, run our business and meet our legal obligations. When we no longer need it, we delete it or keep it in a form that no longer identifies you.</p>

  <h2>Your Choices and Rights</h2>
  <p>You may ask us to show you, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you. You can also unsubscribe from our emails at any time. To make a request, email us at <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under your local privacy laws.</p>

  <h2>Children’s Privacy</h2>
  <p>This website and our programs are for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18. If you believe a child has shared information with us, please contact us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>Links to Other Websites</h2>
  <p>Our website may link to other websites and social media platforms. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, so please read their policies.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page.</p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>Naomi Roe LLC DBA Kingdom Roe Coaching &amp; Consulting<br />P.O. Box 7413, Columbus, MS 39705<br /><a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></p>
</Legal>
